<h2>Asobi Review 1.0 (build 1608) <span class="when">Oct 15, 2026</span></h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Merge a shot into another.</b> When a transition makes two shots one: in Shots on Disk, click the shot to merge from and choose Merge Into. Each of its PLs becomes the other shot&#8217;s next free PL (020&#8217;s PL01 becomes 010&#8217;s PL02), with its versions, records, frame maps, proxies, <code>source_info.txt</code> lines and review movies renamed to match.</li>
<li><b>The shot merged from keeps its work</b>, with a note saying where its plates went; its number is never given again. Written down in <code>00_ADMIN/_RENAMES</code> before anything moves, and undone with Undo Last Merge, like a rename.</li>
<li><b>Undo removes the folders a move made</b>, so a rename or merge undone leaves the shots exactly as they were.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<div class="earlier">Earlier updates</div>
<h3>1.0 (build 1476) <span class="when">Oct 12, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>DPX sequences play.</b> 8, 10, 12 and 16-bit DPX files open and play like any other image sequence, read as the color space set for DPX in Settings, Color.</li>
<li>A tall floating Playlist with thumbnails could stop the app. Fixed.</li>
<li>Small fixes.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1441) <span class="when">Oct 11, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Network is in the Review menu.</b> Review ▸ Network; it was under Window. It is also in the right-click Review menu.</li>
<li><b>A playlist on a network drive no longer slows the window.</b> Whether each clip's file is there is checked in the background.</li>
<li><b>Locate Media… reads a folder in the background.</b> A line above the toolbar says how far it has got.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1430) <span class="when">Oct 11, 2026</span></h3>
