<h2>Asobi Review 1.0 (build 1606) <span class="when">Oct 15, 2026</span></h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Rename a shot.</b> In Shots on Disk, click a row and choose Rename to give its shot another number: its plates, records, frame maps, proxies, <code>source_info.txt</code>, <code>.metadata.json</code>, plate review movies and folder, and the sequence&#8217;s list of names. A number another shot has, or had, is refused.</li>
<li><b>Written down first.</b> Every step is recorded in the job&#8217;s <code>00_ADMIN/_RENAMES</code> before anything moves, and Undo Last Rename puts it all back. Work under <code>work/</code> and <code>renders/</code> is listed, with the scripts that point at the old path, and never changed; Kitsu still calls the shot by its old number.</li>
<li><b>Fixed:</b> a shot whose PL holds two clips (a plate pulled again from another clip) keeps its other PLs and isn&#8217;t pulled again for nothing.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<div class="earlier">Earlier updates</div>
