<h2>Asobi Review 1.0 (build 1604) <span class="when">Oct 15, 2026</span></h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Shots on Disk.</b> Media &#9656; Shots on Disk lists every version folder of the cut&#8217;s sequence, in a window that can join the others as a tab: what is written about it (Asobi, vfx edit, Adopted, or nothing), what the cut on screen says of its shot, and whether its frames agree with that paperwork. Nothing in it changes anything on disk.</li>
<li><b>Verify Paperwork.</b> Each folder&#8217;s frames are checked against their record or <code>source_info.txt</code> line: frame 1001 against the line&#8217;s Source TC, a record&#8217;s first frame against its timecode, a vfx edit line against the cut. A frame out reads &#8220;Off by 2 against its line&#8221;; missing frames, two names in one folder and a PL written for more than one clip are listed too.</li>
<li><b>Filter</b> by Needs Attention, Orphans, Not in This Cut or With Notes, or search by shot, plate or problem; Orphaned Plates&#8230; opens from there.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<div class="earlier">Earlier updates</div>
